{"shortDescription":"By Scott DiSavinoU.S. natural gas futures climbed 2% on Monday on a drop in daily output and an increase in daily liquefied natural gas exports.Front-month gas futures for October delivery NYMEX:NG1! on the New York Mercantile Exchange rose 5.8 cents, or 2.0%, to $2.889 per million British thermal…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Scott DiSavino"]},{"type":"p","children":["U.S. natural gas futures climbed 2% on Monday on a drop in daily output and an increase in daily liquefied natural gas exports."]},{"type":"p","children":["Front-month gas futures for October delivery ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYMEX:NG1!","text":"NYMEX:NG1!"}}," on the New York Mercantile Exchange rose 5.8 cents, or 2.0%, to $2.889 per million British thermal units."]},{"type":"p","children":["Financial firm LSEG said average gas output in the U.S. Lower 48 states rose to 113.4 billion cubic feet per day (bcfd) so far in September, up from a monthly record high of 112.2 bcfd in August."]},{"type":"p","children":["On a daily basis, however, output was on track to decline to a two-week low of 112.8 bcfd on Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Record output and mild spring weather have allowed energy firms to keep the amount of gas in inventory above the five-year (2021-2025) average since March."]},{"type":"p","children":["But with hotter-than-normal weather last week, analysts said the amount of gas in storage likely slid to 3.6% above normal during the week ended September 11, down from 4.8% above normal in the previous week, according to estimates ahead of Thursday's weekly federal inventory report."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meteorologists forecast the weather would remain mostly warmer through September 29, with power generators burning more gas than usual to keep air conditioners running. About 40% of U.S. power generation comes from gas-fired plants."]},{"type":"p","children":["LSEG projected average gas demand in the Lower 48 states, including exports, would slide from 109.5 bcfd this week to 107.3 bcfd next week. Those forecasts were lower than LSEG's outlook on Friday."]},{"type":"p","children":["LNG EXPORTS"]},{"type":"p","children":["Average gas flows to the nine big U.S. LNG export plants rose to 18.3 bcfd so far in September, up from 17.2 bcfd in August, but remained short of the monthly record high of 18.8 bcfd in April."]},{"type":"p","children":["On a daily basis, LNG feedgas was on track to rise to a 20-week high of 18.7 bcfd on Friday."]},{"type":"p","children":["U.S. energy firm Berkshire Hathaway Energy, however, has told customers that it plans to shut its 0.8-bcfd Cove Point LNG export plant in Maryland for a couple of weeks of annual maintenance starting around September 19."]},{"type":"p","children":["The U.S. became the world's biggest LNG exporter in 2023, surpassing Australia and Qatar, as surging global prices fed demand for more low-cost U.S. gas."]},{"type":"p","children":["Around the world, gas traded at 44-month highs of around $28 per mmBtu at the Dutch Title Transfer Facility ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"ICEENDEX:TFM1!","text":"ICEENDEX:TFM1!"}}," benchmark in Europe and $25 at the Japan-Korea Marker (JKMc1) benchmark in Asia."]},{"type":"p","children":["Global gas prices have spiked in recent years primarily due to supply disruptions linked to Russia's ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/ukraine-russia-war/","linkText":"invasion of Ukraine"}}," in 2022 and the U.S.-Israeli ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/iran/","linkText":"war with Iran"}}," this year."]},{"type":"p","children":["Prices in the U.S. have not reacted much to the war in Iran because the U.S. produces all the gas it consumes domestically and U.S. LNG companies are already liquefying as much fuel as they can."]},{"type":"p","children":["No matter how high global gas prices go, the U.S. cannot export much more LNG until units under construction enter service in coming months and years."]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Week ended Sep 11 Forecast"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Week ended  Sep 4 Actual"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Year ago Sep 11"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Five-year average (2021-2025) Sep 11"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["U.S. weekly natgas storage change (bcf):"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+42"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+40"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+87"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+74"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["U.S. total natgas in storage (bcf):"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3,296"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3,254"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3,420"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3,180"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["U.S. total storage versus 5-year average"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+3.6%"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+4.8%"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row"